  'bronkhorstspruit-water-plant-still-shut-2026-11-16',
  'Bronkhorstspruit water plant still shut as mud clouds supply',
  'Utilities', '2026-11-16', 'IOL', 'https://iol.co.za/news/south-africa/2026-11-16-tshwane-temporarily-shuts-bronkhorstspruit-water-plant-works-due-to-low-raw-water-quality/',
  'The City of Tshwane says the Bronkhorstspruit Water Treatment Plant has stayed off since 16 November because incoming raw water is too muddy to treat.',
  'The City of Tshwane temporarily shut down the Bronkhorstspruit Water Treatment Plant in the early hours of 16 November, saying the raw water flowing into it carried too much mud and silt to treat safely. The plant supplies water to several communities, including Bronkhorstspruit, Zithobeni, Rethabiseng, Ekangala, Ekandustria and Sokhulumi.

City spokespeople said the pause was meant to stop poor-quality raw water from compromising the plant''s output, describing the incoming supply as far too cloudy for effective treatment. Officials added that no restart date could be given yet, and promised more updates once conditions allowed treatment to resume.

As of 20 November, the plant remained offline, even though the incoming raw water looked somewhat clearer on the morning of 17 November, according to the city. Residents in the affected areas have been told to avoid drinking the tap water until the city and Rand Water confirm it is safe again, and to use it only to flush toilets rather than for cooking, bathing, brushing teeth or washing dishes and laundry.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://iol.co.za/news/south-africa/2026-11-16-tshwane-temporarily-shuts-bronkhorstspruit-water-plant-works-due-to-low-raw-water-quality/", "https://www.citizen.co.za/news/bronkhorstspruit-water-plant-shut-down-what-tshwane-residents-should-know-about-supply/", "https://pretorianews.co.za/news/2026-11-20-city-of-tshwane-issues-temba-boil-water-warning-and-bronkhorstspruit-plant-remains-shutdown/"]',
  'agent'
